=== (1) THE GRADIENT CHECK THAT REDIRECTED THIS ROUND — recorded, not dropped ===
  the shared 4-item sexual-strictness scale I meant to use: Cronbach α = **0.694** (n=1246), against the sanction indices' KR-20 of 0.802 and 0.789
  ⇒ **equalising the norm ruler would have equalised it DOWNWARD**, cost half the sample, and put `homosex` on both sides. **A different estimand dressed as a control.**

=== (2) THE SAMPLE-DEFINITION SWEEP — the rows, not the items ===
  #888 as published (all 7 ab items)     n= 2480  **Δ +0.051**
  only the TRIO required                 n= 2586  **Δ +0.033**
  #883 base (single-binary rule)         n= 2694  **Δ +0.035**
  + requires teensex (drops 2008)        n= 1266  **Δ +0.024**
  + requires all 4 norm items            n= 1246  **Δ +0.023**
  **completeness-rule spread = 0.028**

=== (3) LEAVE-ONE-WAVE-OUT — is the pooled number an average over heterogeneous cells? ===
  drop 1991: Δ **+0.079**   |   wave 1991 alone: Δ +0.022 (n=668)
  drop 1998: Δ **+0.055**   |   wave 1998 alone: Δ +0.037 (n=614)
  drop 2008: Δ **+0.022**   |   wave 2008 alone: Δ +0.156 (n=558)
  drop 2018: Δ **+0.059**   |   wave 2018 alone: Δ +0.084 (n=640)
  **LOWO spread = 0.057** · the wave whose removal moves Δ most is **2008** (+0.051 → +0.022)

=== (4) THE NULL — kind of null NAMED: a CONSTANT-Δ resampling null ===
  respondents drawn within each wave from the POOLED table ⇒ true Δ identical in every wave
  null LOWO spread: median **0.025** · 95th **0.046**
  observed **0.057** ⇒ above what four noisy waves give for free: **True**

=== (5) POSITIVE CONTROL — plant a between-wave difference, floor and ceiling MEASURED ===
  g=0.00  planted LOWO spread = 0.029
  g=0.05  planted LOWO spread = 0.045
  g=0.10  planted LOWO spread = 0.056
  g=0.20  planted LOWO spread = 0.083
  g=0.40  planted LOWO spread = 0.115
  measured FLOOR 0.029 · CEILING 0.115 ⇒ the null's 95th (0.046) lies strictly between them: True
  => positive control **PASS** — monotone True, **and at g=0 it does not fire**

=== (6) NEGATIVE CONTROL — a global permutation. This zero SHOULD be zero ===
  null mean +0.0006 -> **PASS**

